[`eth_fillTransaction`](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/5fa696822d94d70263360001a4083eb861fd1e50/internal/ethapi/api.go#L1784-L1802) discards frame fields and can reject the request as empty contract creation.

Example for a funded sender on a frame-enabled chain:

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1,
  "method": "eth_fillTransaction",
  "params": [{
    "type": "0x6",
    "from": "0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111",
    "frames": [
      { "mode": "0x1", "flags": "0x3", "stateGas": "0x0" },
      { "mode": "0x2", "stateGas": "0x0" }
    ],
    "signatures": [{ "scheme": "0x1" }]
  }]
}
```

Return a filled type-`0x6` transaction under `tx`, following https://github.com/ethereum/execution-apis/pull/907. Fill envelope fields and frame defaults, estimate omitted gas limits, preserve explicit zero and signature placeholders, and use `from`, `executionGas`, and `stateGas`.

Source review of `frames-devnet-0` at `5fa6968`, against proposal `31a8c4e`. Example not live-tested.

